<%# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    VIEW: views/resources.ejs
    CONTENT FRAGMENT ONLY — no <head>, <nav>, or <footer>.

    ZERO NEW CSS — uses only the .res-section / .res-inner /
    .res-head / .res-eyebrow / .res-title / .res-divider /
    .res-grid / .res-card / .res-card-num / .res-card-title-wrap /
    .res-card-title / .res-card-sep / .res-card-btn components
    that already exist in your stylesheet, plus #why (dark hero
    background) and your shared .hero-eyebrow / .hero-h1 /
    .hero-sub / .btn-primary / .btn-secondary classes.

    HOW CARDS OPEN URLS
    ───────────────────
    Every .res-card is a plain <a> tag with target="_blank"
    and rel="noopener" — clicking the whole card opens the URL
    in a new tab. The .res-card-btn inside is a visual affordance
    only (pointer-events: none so it doesn't double-fire), styled
    exactly as your existing stylesheet expects.

    ADDING MORE RESOURCES
    ─────────────────────
    Each category is a separate .res-section block. To add a new
    resource entry, copy any .res-card block and update:
      - href     → the URL to open
      - emoji    → a fitting icon
      - title    → the resource name
      - btn text → "View", "Download", "Watch", etc.
    The card count badge (01, 02 …) is cosmetic only — renumber
    or remove as you like.

    EXPECTED LOCALS (all optional)
    ────────────────────────────────
    None required. This is static content. If you later want to
    drive this from a database (title, url, category, type per
    row), the EJS loops map directly onto the markup structure.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ %>

<!-- ══ PAGE HERO ══ -->
<section id="why">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hero-eyebrow"><div class="dot"></div> Knowledge Centre</div>
    <h1 class="hero-h1" style="font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,46px)">Resources</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">Everything you need to evaluate, deploy, and get the most out of the solutions we distribute — events, datasheets, case studies, guides, and more.</p>
    <div class="hero-stats" style="margin-bottom:32px">
      <div class="hero-stat"><div class="num">1</div><div class="lbl">Category live now</div></div>
      <div class="hero-stat"><div class="num">More</div><div class="lbl">Coming soon</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══ CATEGORY: EVENTS & WEBINARS ══ -->
<section class="res-section" id="events-webinars">
